{"result":"{
  "id": "18363",
  "key": "SFCC-197",
  "summary": "Product Image Management",
  "description": "\\*\\*As a\\*\\* Merchandiser,\n\\*\\*I want\\*\\* to merchandize the product images within SFCC,\n\\*\\*so that\\*\\* the storefront can reliably display optimised product imagery.\n----\nProduct images are synced into SFCC through the MuleSoft Product feed. Video covered in separate user story — see [SFCC-188](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-188) and [SFCC-302](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-302) .\nWe need to categorize images in BM so that they can correctly render in the right pages:\n|\\*\\*Image View Type\\*\\*|\\*\\*M2 Name (for reference)\\*\\*|\\*\\*Description\\*\\*|\n|---|---|---|\n|Flat Item Image|Base|Item/flat lay view — background less (PNG), required due to dynamic background colour. Primary on PLP, secondary on PDP.\nThis one is also used as the colour swatch selector image on PDP. Please note - not always primary on PDP - for example, on accessories this might be different.|\n|Detail Image|Colour Swatch Images|Close up shot - will be used in the colour swatch selector on the expanded image gallery on PDP.|\n|Model Image|Model Image|Model view (hero image) and a way to tag a video or image as relevant to show on hover - e.g. it will show on a product card’s hover state on PLP. Often primary on PDP, not always|\n|Hidden|Hidden|Way to tag an image as hidden - this means you see the image on roll over (like on PLP, maybe home page) but once you click into the PDP then the image gallery no longer shows that one. Used today sometimes for runway styles.|\n|Product Styling Image|Product Styling Image|This image will be used for the Shop the look picture - smaller component.|\n|Front View|N/A|This view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images|\n|Side View|N/A|This view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images|\n|Back View|N/A|This view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images|\n|Campaign|N/A|This image will be used for the Shop the look picture - larger component.|\n|Runway|N/A|This image will be used for the Shop the look picture - larger component.|\nExtra information:\n- We need to have one canonical view type folder in SFCC that gathers the entire image gallery and determines the order of the image gallery on PDP (suggested is View Type = Large). The display order should be adjustable.\n- Manual swatches for accessories - content team has to upload swatch images for these.\n- Runway / Campaign imagery are also there - they come at the end of the carousel.\n- We can use the image view type to prepopulate the alt text - so combination of view type  product name (SFCC-31 )\nMaintaining documentation here on Confluence so we can discuss with the MuleSoft team later: [04.4.5 Product Images — View Types & MuleSoft Mapping Rules - Adobe SFCC - Confluence](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/450068481/04.4.5ProductImagesViewTypesMuleSoftMappingRules)",
